<title>POLAND: Polish wheat prices slip, barley flat last week.</title>
<headline>Polish wheat prices slip, barley flat last week.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish Agriculture Ministry said in a statement that wheat prices eased, barley was flat and rye prices rose during last week's grain auctions.</p>
<p>POLISH FARM AUCTION PRICES (AVERAGE)</p>
<p>  Product   week to March 1    previous week   yr/yr growth</p>
<p>   Wheat	55.71 zl/q	 56.53 zl/q	  3.7 pct</p>
<p>   Rye	  42.47 zl/q	 42.04 zl/q	 23.5 pct</p>
<p>   Barley     49.65 zl/q	 49.65 zl/q	  6.4 pct</p>
<p>NOTE: zl/q = zlotys per quintal.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
